WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.980
We don't know where your 
wife, Miharu-san, went

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.980
after she left the flower shop 
she works at around 7:30 PM.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.650
We're certain that the riverbed where

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.760
her body was found is 
where her murder took place.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.950
We're uncertain about the details,

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.080
but she was hit repeatedly on 
the head with a blunt object,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.490
and her arms show signs that 
she tried to defend herself.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.550
The suspect hit her from behind,

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.500
and then murdered her when she
turned around and tried to fight back.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.080
There were no signs of 
her belongings being stolen.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.430
We believe the motive 
was a deep-seated grudge.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.560
We haven't found the murder weapon yet.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.260
We're talking about the night 
of Saturday, September 12th.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:42.330
It's been over a year since I divorced Miharu.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.170
I haven't seen her or had 
any contact with her since.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.070
I didn't know she was 
working at a flower shop,

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.080
or that she was living in the 
next prefecture over, until now.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.030
By the way, about the reason you divorced...

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.530
Publicly, it's said to be because 
Miharu-san was unfaithful,

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.230
but I hear it's actually 
because she tried to kill you.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.740
How did you know about that?

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.160
It happened last March.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.480
I was about to drive to work,

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:15.570
and she put a sleeping drug 
in my usual energy drink.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.060
Have a good day.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.070
Thanks.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:21.990
Hello?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.200
Muroi

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:26.200
I left my house while on the phone, so I 
ended up putting the bottle in my pocket,

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.210
and just left.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:31.170
The phone call was from one of my clients,

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.740
and I had to stop by the 
office to get some papers.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.950
I only survived due to 
a string of lucky breaks.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.770
The one most likely to have put the 
sleeping drug in the drink was my wife.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:52.460
When I looked into it, 
I found that she was cheating on me.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.250
When I showed her what I'd found,

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.230
she admitted to my attempted murder.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.650
If things had gone as she planned,

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.850
the sleeping drug would've taken 
effect while I was on the freeway.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:06.810
Apparently, she was after my fortune 
and planned to marry her lover.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:10.830
But how do the police know about this?

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:13.420
I haven't told anyone about it,

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.920
and Miharu told me that she 
kept it a secret from her lover.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:20.550
Before we answer, why didn't 
you take your wife to court?

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:26.060
Attempted murder, apparently, 
isn't much of an offense.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:30.640
Ah, I heard that you were almost killed 
by your friend back in college, as well.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.990
Yes, and that's why I know 
it'd all just be in vain.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.650
I married my wife because I loved her.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.100
Fortunately, I was left without a scratch.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.350
I'm also at fault for making her 
feel like she needed another man

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:46.580
because I was always at work.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.040
Yet there was the fact that 
she had cheated on you,

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.790
and solid proof that she tried to murder you,

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:56.100
so Miharu-san had no choice 
but to accept the divorce.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:04:00.220
And still, you split your fortune with her.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.840
I had the right do what I wanted with it.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:05.590
I couldn't have her deciding to retaliate 
because I treated her too coldly.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.870
That is a valid concern.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.340
It appears the person 
Miharu-san was cheating with

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:13.020
wanted to break up with her 
right after the divorce.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.100
I'm sure it worked in your favor financially.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.690
You might be far kinder than you look.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.900
But that's not how Miharu-san saw it.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.270
Miharu-san had hidden a letter in her house

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:28.750
saying that if she died in a strange way,

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:32.600
you must have been the one who 
killed her and to arrest you right away.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:36.170
That's also where she had written 
about attempting to kill you,

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.460
which led to your divorce.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.550
Without that,

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:43.670
we never would've known what really 
happened between you and Miharu-san.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:49.180
It doesn't matter what Miharu wrote. 
I had no reason to kill her.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:54.270
Miharu-san genuinely felt that you 
would seek revenge against her.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:55.800
Of course you'd resent her,

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:59.770
since she tried to kill you 
and take all of your money.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:03.820
Yet you never reported that to the police 
and settled for just divorcing her,

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.570
and even split your fortune with her.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:09.530
You even lied about the reason for 
the divorce, protecting her reputation.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.990
People can only be so generous.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.660
Miharu-san considered it to be creepy.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.580
<i>It's true. That's so generous, it's creepy.</i>

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:22.380
That's why she suspected 
that it was just camouflage

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.090
so that you could kill her later.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:28.830
Miharu-san had written in her letter 
that you intentionally made it look

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.010
like you divorced on good terms,

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.720
so that when you killed her, 
no one would suspect you.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.510
That's why you didn't tell 
anyone about the murder attempt,

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:40.770
and make it sound like you're also at fault.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.360
Your accusations are baseless.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:47.330
I'm not so spiteful that I'd waste 
so much time and effort on revenge.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:51.430
<i>If I was that passionate, 
I would
't be holed up here.</i>

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.710
<i>It doesn't matter. Whatever I 
say back will just be in vain.</i>

00:05:55.710 --> 00:06:00.760
I see that your friend who 
tried to kill you is also dead.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:04.000
Three years after he attempted 
to murder you in the mountains.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.510
He was in a car accident.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:09.390
Apparently, yes. At least, that's what I 
heard, though I don't know the details.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:12.370
We looked into that matter just in case,

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:16.610
but there was no evidence that you were 
involved, and no one suspected you.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:17.660
Of course not.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.740
However, when Miharu-san 
found out about this,

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.300
she thought that you had done it,

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.940
which made her even more wary of you.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.610
She thought you'd seek revenge 
against her in the same way.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:30.550
That's why she hid a letter 
confessing her own crimes.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.620
And you actually believe that?

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.330
When she died, Miharu-san's palm

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.080
had letters written on it with marker.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:43.460
She died with her fist clenched, 
so the suspect probably didn't notice.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:46.460
It appeared she wrote it very quickly 
without looking at her hand.

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:49.590
The marker she used has not been found.

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:53.840
She might've thrown it away somewhere 
so that the suspect wouldn't notice.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.850
But what could be read as "Masayu" 
was written on her hand in katakana.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:58.850
<b>Masayu</b>

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:01.660
I believe that your name is Masayuki.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:05.030
She may have stopped in 
the middle of writing it,

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.700
fearing the suspect would catch on.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:10.690
If it was incomplete, there's no guarantee 
that she was trying to write "ki" next.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.170
You are correct. She may have 
been trying to write "ko,"

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:16.380
but it ended up looking like "yu."

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:18.330
By the way...

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:23.190
Where were you on September 
12th from 8 PM to 10 PM?

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:26.840
September... 12th...

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:29.170
Take a look at this.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:34.190
This is a picture from a security 
camera at the mall closest to here.

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:37.720
The date is September 4th. 
Eight days before the incident.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:42.300
It appears to be you and a woman who 
looks like Miharu-san in the picture.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:47.900
You mentioned that you hadn't seen 
her once since your divorce, but...

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.990
This woman may look like 
Miharu, but it isn't her.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:54.240
Then just who might she be?

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:02.920
Would you come with us to 
the nearest police station?

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:13.630
<i>Should I return to the mountains for now?</i>

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.570
<i>No. I guess I'll wait for him.</i>

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:32.600
Miha—

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.200
Ah, you took quite a while.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:43.210
To think that she'd continue to 
cause you trouble after her death...

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.210
What an awful woman.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.210
<b>Crystal</b>

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.210
And then there's you.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.210
<b>Crystal
High Ball</b>

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.420
If you talked to your neighbors 
every now and then,

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:52.170
you may have actually had an alibi.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:55.230
You're right, but it's not 
like I don't have an alibi.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:59.770
September 12th at 8 PM
was just around the time

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:02.350
that I was eating tempura with you.

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:06.750
Ooh! That day, we ate tempura 
and drank alcohol into the night,

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.480
and I went home in the morning.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:12.860
Then there's no way you're the suspect! 
Everything's taken care of!

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:18.170
But it's not like I can hand a Yuki-Onna 
over to the police as my alibi.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.400
When they asked for my alibi,

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:23.080
I should've just immediately 
said that I didn't have one,

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:26.540
but I ended up saying that it's 
not like I didn't have one.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.790
That pause made the police suspect me more.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:32.300
Even so, you are innocent!

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.750
You'd be cleared of any suspicion!

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:39.260
But the image from the security camera 
has put me in a bad situation,

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:42.710
so they're going to suspect me, 
no matter what I say.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:47.940
Do I look like your former wife?

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.230
If you stood next to her, 
there'd be differences,

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:51.610
but you do look alike.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:57.320
Why in the world did you marry 
a woman who looks like me?

00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:59.310
Who knows?

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:05.080
Perhaps I couldn't forget what I saw

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:07.830
when I looked up while buried in the snow.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:11.340
The white figure I saw 
on the brink of death...

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:14.900
No matter how much I was 
betrayed, that didn't waver.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.930
That was the one thing 
that hadn't betrayed me.

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:23.710
Ah, shit. I was planning on 
never letting that slip...

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:26.040
But at the same time, 
it's tiring to keep up this ruse.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.190
What do I even say to this?

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:32.940
If that was the case, I'm sure your former 
wife took issue with that, as well.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.400
She might've felt like she was being 
compared to someone the whole time.

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:38.280
I feel bad about it.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.820
That's why I couldn't blame 
her for cheating on me,

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.660
and I tried to be mindful during our divorce.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:45.380
But attempted murder is going a bit far.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:50.620
I can't explain my alibi or about 
the woman I was with to the police.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.170
And because of that, their suspicions 
that I did it are growing.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:54.880
It feels like I fell into a trap.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:02.540
Are you in a worse situation because 
I cannot serve as a witness for you?

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.600
Things are looking pretty bad...

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:07.600
But thankfully, I have time and money.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:12.260
I'm going to find the real culprit 
before they try to tie me down.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:16.140
Then I'll be able to prove my innocence.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:17.480
Hey, Masayuki—

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.880
There's no other way.

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:20.460
Wait...

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:22.790
Sorry, but I'm not going 
to be home for a while.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:25.080
Wait. Do you have any idea how to find them?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.530
It's better than being holed up here.

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:28.900
Wait, wait, wait!

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:32.710
I'm stocked up on booze and food, 
and I'll leave you some cash, too,

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:33.880
so you can do as you please.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.090
I'm telling you to wait!

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:41.470
I only see failure in your future 
if you go about this with no leads.

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:44.000
I'm sure the police have 
their eyes on you, as well.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:47.430
I will help you, so stop trying 
to do everything alone!

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:52.060
I know of your innocence! 
I will not let them capture you!

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.970
Come, now, and drink! Eat!

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:57.770
Have some okonomiyaki that I made.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.300
It's half raw...

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:01.780
I-I figured that's better 
than it being burnt.

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:03.280
After you eat, it's time for bed.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.240
You even get a beautiful 
woman to lie with you.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:09.240
Listen carefully, Masayuki.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.950
Rest for now.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.960
<i>You say that, but what 
am I supposed to do now?</i>

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:18.920
<i>As always, her hand is white as can be.</i>

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:21.740
I know!

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:25.260
This is the perfect time to rely on our lady!

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:29.510
She'll be able to help you 
and find the true culprit!

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.520
Is that even going to work?

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:35.600
<i>The police didn't keep bothering 
me like I thought they would.</i>

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:35.600
<b>Nine

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:38.610
<i>It's already been over a 
week since they showed up.</i>

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.080
Masayuki!

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:44.770
Our ladyship has arrived! 
We must go see her immediately!

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:46.360
Wh-Where are we going?

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.820
Deep into the mountains.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.010
Don't fall!

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:00.960
My lady!

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.970
<i>Th-This girl...</i>

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:15.460
<i>is her ladyship, the Goddess of Wisdom?</i>

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:26.990
<b>The Yuki-Onna's Alibi</b>

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:32.620
My lady! I humbly thank you 
for listening to my request!

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:36.250
It's quite all right. 
This is my duty, after all.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.100
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:47.130
I am the Goddess of Wisdom to yokai, 
ayakashi, spectres, and demons.

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.410
My name is Iwanaga Kotoko.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:51.240
I am here upon Yuki-Onna's request,

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:54.330
to resolve the incident 
that you are involved in.

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:57.870
I'm Muroi Masayuki. 
Thank you for coming all this way—

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:00.870
I could've just gone to your house,

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:04.580
but I'm sure it might've been troublesome 
for someone like me to come by your home.

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:05.190
Hup.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:09.900
It's a bit chilly here, but suitable
for us to talk for a while.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:11.950
Did you come here alone?

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:15.490
I heard that you had a boyfriend. 
Where might he be?

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:20.290
Well, I invited him to come along, of course...

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:24.960
But he had the nerve to decline, 
saying he had to work construction tonight.

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:28.020
The nerve, prioritizing the 
construction of a tunnel at night

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.130
over his cute girlfriend...

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:32.870
Of course, he is a grad student, 
so I realize he may need money.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:36.200
I told him my family could pay for that, 
but he just wouldn't listen.

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:37.480
And because of that,

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.220
I've been forced to buy a bento and 
drink from a local convenience store,

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:43.440
and had the monsters escort 
me up to these mountains.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:48.190
Previously, he would make me 
a warm bento and pork soup,

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:53.210
so why would he leave me in a situation 
where I must eat cold tonkatsu?!

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.700
Oh, I beg your pardon. I went off-topic.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:00.080
I can't stay mad about this forever.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:04.730
I've looked into the basic details 
about you and your incident.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:08.340
To think that having Yuki-Onna as a witness 
makes them suspect you even more...

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:11.210
It may show that there is always 
a chance of unexpected danger

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:14.350
when an ill-prepared human 
gets involved with an ayakashi.

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:19.140
This man is innocent, but has been put 
in a difficult situation because of me.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:23.130
He may look rough around the edges, 
but he is not a bad human.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.610
I implore you to assist us.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:28.070
It's not your fault. 
Isn't that right, Muroi-san?

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:31.150
It's all due to my unworthiness. 
She has done nothing wrong.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.420
Then again,

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:35.910
it must be unpleasant to have 
everything work so perfectly against you.

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:38.290
Like how Yuki-Onna is the 
witness who can provide an alibi,

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.130
and how she's in the security 
camera image with you

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.000
and being mistaken 
for your murdered wife.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:46.750
The predicament that you're in almost 
sounds like the plot of some play.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.970
But doesn't that make you want 
to proceed with some doubt?

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:57.310
Is your alibi actually trustworthy even 
if we can affirm the existence of yokai?

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:58.830
When it comes to yokai and humans,

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:01.310
their lifespans and sense 
of time are different.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:03.910
They don't usually use calendars,

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:08.820
and they don't usually specifically 
know what day it is like humans do.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.530
Now, then, Yuki-Onna.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:14.260
Can you tell me exactly what 
month and day today is?

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:16.910
Huh? Um...

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:21.080
Is it, like... the beginning of October? Um...

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:23.730
If Muroi-san said the 12th, 
when the incident occurred,

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:25.750
was at <i>that</i> time on <i>that</i> day,

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:29.390
Yuki-Onna would simply assume, 
"Ah, so it was that day."

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:32.760
Even if it were actually the 11th or 13th,

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:35.140
she wouldn't specifically 
be able to tell them apart.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:40.520
If you had felt like just giving her the 
wrong date, she would be easily deceived.

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:44.640
Meaning it was very possible for you 
to kill your ex-wife on the 12th.

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:50.150
You don't have a solid alibi, 
even with Yuki-Onna as your witness.

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:52.370
Even with the security camera footage,

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:55.070
you could've figured out Miharu-san's 
usual routine beforehand,

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:58.360
and could have purposely been 
filmed with Yuki-Onna

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:02.650
at a time when Miharu-san's 
whereabouts were unknown.

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:05.670
You can't say you just happened 
to be caught on camera.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.250
Can you wholeheartedly say that your alibi

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.300
or that footage weren't 
completely deliberate?

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:13.010
What could I possibly gain 
from them being deliberate?

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:15.240
You make it sound as if I made up my alibi

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:17.710
and purposely made sure that 
security camera footage existed,

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:21.010
but that'd only put me at a disadvantage. 
I'd gain nothing from it.

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:23.880
At this rate, I'm going to 
be arrested by the police,

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:26.060
and I have no way of proving my innocence.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.770
But you do have something to gain.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:31.270
Yuki-Onna's absolute trust in you.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:32.690
What?

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:37.400
If Yuki-Onna believes in you, 
she'd have no reason to doubt your innocence.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:38.620
And because of that,

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.820
she'd think, "I'll do anything to help him."

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:44.040
"I want to be of use to him."

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:48.660
If she's convinced that you were 
at a disadvantage because of her,

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:51.780
she'd take your side without any hesitation.

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:56.050
You have countless people that you'd 
consider worthwhile to exact revenge upon.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.410
Your friend that tried to kill you,

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:02.560
your ex-wife, and your colleagues that 
betrayed you and took your company.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.860
The first two have died,

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:06.630
but the others remain.

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:09.560
You were removed from your position, 
and they took your title.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.520
There must be more than two or three.

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:14.750
And it'd be quite a chore to 
finish killing all of them.

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:18.990
But what if you got Yuki-Onna 
to be on your side?

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.490
If you were to be arrested 
because of Miharu-san's incident,

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:23.730
and you said, "My former 
colleagues were scared that

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:25.290
their corruption would be tracked down,

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.500
and I found out that they 
had set up a trap for me.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:31.500
I can't prove my innocence, nor can 
I track down their corruption.

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.940
Could you exact revenge upon them for me?"

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:36.760
If you had earnestly asked her to do that,

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:41.010
Yuki-Onna would've probably done just that 
because she believes in your innocence.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:44.510
She is a yokai that exists outside 
the laws and morals of humans.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:48.770
She would probably freeze them to 
death because she believed in you.

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:57.980
<i>Is she trembling because 
of her ladyship's theory?</i>

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:03.240
<i>Yuki-Onna was relying on her lady.</i>

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.540
Exacting revenge while 
being completely safe...

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:09.710
For that final goal,

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.440
you premeditated the murder of Miharu-san,

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:15.150
purposely put yourself in a situation 
to have the police suspect you,

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:17.210
and tried to gain the trust of Yuki-Onna.

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:18.720
Am I wrong?

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:24.280
<i>I never had any hope in 
this Goddess of Wisdom...</i>

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.510
<i>But I can't believe she managed to 
come up with such a fabrication.</i>

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:31.010
It'd be a futile plan that'd just 
leave me walking on thin ice.

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:34.510
Even if I were able to exact my revenge, 
if I'd be put on trial for Miharu's murder

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:36.540
and found guilty, there's no point.

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:39.530
But you have a yokai like 
Yuki-Onna on your side.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:41.230
After you exact your revenge,

00:19:41.230 --> 00:19:43.280
you can just say you came up with a way out,

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:46.030
and have the Yuki-Onna take 
some kind of action again.

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:49.790
You could have her go to the mall, 
get into the security camera footage,

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:53.040
and then have a lawyer you 
hired look up that footage.

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:55.140
If you can prove that a woman

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:58.540
resembling Miharu-san frequented
the area even after her death,

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:01.130
the basis of the police's suspicion 
against you would fall apart.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:04.090
Even if prosecution has 
probable evidence against you,

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:06.390
Yuki-Onna could just steal 
it before the trial,

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:08.100
and hide it.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.000
It wouldn't be hard to make 
it seem you're not guilty,

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.430
or to have them drop the case.

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:16.250
If you were just striking a minor deal 
with a yokai, I'd easily advert my eyes...

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:18.430
But I cannot allow you 
to selfishly control a yokai

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:21.530
to do your bidding to 
satisfy your own interests.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:25.740
That act could destroy the 
laws of both man and yokai.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:28.520
My lady!

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:31.930
I do beg your pardon,

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:35.170
but this man is not capable of 
concocting such an evil plan.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:38.120
It's true...

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:42.170
It's true that I believe 
in this man's innocence,

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:46.300
and I probably would not hesitate 
to kill another for him.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:49.230
And I do not doubt your great 
wisdom or keen judgment...

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:51.640
But though this man may look 
rough around the edges,

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:55.020
he possesses a truly kind heart,

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:57.650
and is incapable of hating others!

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:00.530
Otherwise, how could he have 
been betrayed so many times,

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:04.030
so hurt, and unable to trust 
another human being anymore?

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:06.410
Please...

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:08.660
I beg you to reconsider!

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:23.880
Yes, yes, I know.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:26.590
I'm very aware that Muroi-san 
is not the culprit.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:28.930
Everything I just uttered was a lie.

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:33.890
Huh?

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.280
What did you say?

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:38.650
There were a number of holes in my theory,

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:41.900
but if you were just trying 
to gain Yuki-Onna's trust,

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:44.900
I'm sure the two of you would've moved 
on to making babies quite a while ago.

00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:47.110
Because having relations like that

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:49.650
is the easiest way to convince 
her to take your side.

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:50.910
The utter lack of morals...

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:56.010
Well, I heard that you've been turning 
down all of Yuki-Onna's advances.

00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:58.580
I was in complete awe of your cowardice.

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:01.970
Such a person would never be able 
to devise nor execute the plan

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:03.320
I just laid out.

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:06.170
That's why my theory has no leg to stand on.

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:10.660
Then why did you bother 
making up all those lies?

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:12.850
That was far too cruel 
to be considered a joke.

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:14.850
It was to enlighten you.

00:22:15.660 --> 00:22:17.600
Yuki-Onna went as far as to argue with me

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:21.360
to defend you, even though 
I am a goddess to her.

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:23.610
That required a great deal of courage.

00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:27.020
She went as far as defying 
a goddess for your sake.

00:22:29.480 --> 00:22:34.190
She may be a yokai, but she believes 
in you and has put her full faith in you.

00:22:34.190 --> 00:22:38.490
You may be too scared to believe in 
people again because you were hurt,

00:22:38.490 --> 00:22:40.550
but your existence is that meaningful.

00:22:41.090 --> 00:22:43.300
I think it's about time you made a new start.

00:22:45.860 --> 00:22:47.740
<i>What the hell am I doing?</i>

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:51.050
<i>It's true that I've been hurt and 
became so tired that I ran away.</i>

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:53.890
<i>But I was reunited with Yuki-Onna 
and was able to find peace.</i>

00:22:54.510 --> 00:22:57.450
<i>But a part of me felt guilty.</i>

00:22:57.450 --> 00:23:00.590
<i>I was a coward who was terrified 
to interact with others again,</i>

00:23:00.590 --> 00:23:02.290
<i>and I couldn't muster my courage.</i>

00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:05.530
I can't say I'm too concerned 
with what happens to you,

00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:10.030
but as the Goddess of Wisdom, 
I must see Yuki-Onna's request through.

00:23:10.370 --> 00:23:15.150
Just solving this case isn't 
going to save you, is it?

00:23:15.150 --> 00:23:17.410
I'm sorry. You're absolutely right.

00:23:20.700 --> 00:23:22.130
Sorry for the trouble I've caused.

00:23:28.270 --> 00:23:31.730
So what about Miharu's murder case?

00:23:31.730 --> 00:23:36.510
If the true culprit isn't apprehended, 
I'm still in hot water.

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:38.770
I know who the true culprit is.

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:42.480
There's really no need to rush,

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:46.190
but I guess I can tell you how 
that will also be resolved.

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:49.980
To be continued
